body:
Filed out of the contract review of objectui#8914 (card objectui#8310), rider F6, at the reviewer's instruction. **Unassigned and ungraded on purpose** — `domain:*`, priority and type are triage's to set. ⛔ Deliberately NOT repaired in objectui#8914: it is pre-existing and outside that ruling's scope.

## The predicate

`packages/components/src/renderers/layout/page.tsx`:

```ts
function containsTitledPageHeader(nodes: unknown, depth = 0): boolean {
  if (!Array.isArray(nodes) || depth > 6) return false;
  ...
}

function pageHeaderOwnsTitle(schema: PageNodeSchema): boolean {
  const regionNodes = (schema.regions ?? []).flatMap((r: any) => r?.components ?? []);
  return (
    containsTitledPageHeader(regionNodes) ||
    containsTitledPageHeader((schema as any).body) ||
    containsTitledPageHeader((schema as any).children)
  );
}
```

The helper's first line is an early `false` for anything that is not an array. `pageHeaderOwnsTitle` hands it `schema.body` directly. So a page whose `body` is ONE `page:header` node — not a list containing one — takes the early return, `pageHeaderOwnsTitle` answers `false`, and `PageRenderer` emits its own `h1` next to the one the header renders.

That is exactly the broken document outline objectui#3434 closed: one document, two `h1` elements with the same name, announced twice by a screen reader and visibly duplicated. The rule is intact for the list arity and for `regions[].components`; only the bare-node channel misses it.

## Why it is worth a card now, when it was only a report bullet before

Before objectui#8310, `PageNodeSchema.body` was declared `SchemaNode[]`, so the single-node form was refused by the declaration and this path was reachable only by an author who bypassed the type. objectui#8914 widened the key to `SchemaNode | SchemaNode[]` on both faces, matching `BaseSchema` and the renderer's own `FlatContent` fallback — which has always normalized a bare node into a one-element list. The single-node arity is now a **declared, first-class authored shape**, and the root `README.md` flagship example authors it. The delegation check is the one reader on that path that did not follow.

## Second half — a cast that is no longer load-bearing

`pageHeaderOwnsTitle` passes `(schema as any).body` and `(schema as any).children`. The parameter is `unknown`, so neither cast buys anything; the `body` one is doubly redundant now that `PageNodeSchema` declares the key with the arity the helper is being asked about. Removing them is how the type face would have surfaced this in the first place.

## Suggested shape of the repair, for triage — not a ruling

Normalize at the boundary rather than at each call site: have `containsTitledPageHeader` accept one node or a list (the same `Array.isArray` widening `FlatContent` already performs), so `regions`, `body` and `children` are all judged by one rule. Then drop the two `as any`. A pin belongs with it: a `page` whose `body` is a single titled `page:header` must render exactly one `h1`.

## Measurement honesty

Read-derived, from the predicate quoted above — no runtime reproduction was executed in this round. It was reached independently twice: by the implementing seat while writing objectui#8914 (recorded there as `noted, not filed`) and by the contract reviewer of that PR. A browser or jsdom repro is a step the fixing seat should take first, so the pin is written against an observed duplicate rather than against the source reading.
